 "The §0 tactic allows you to prove intermediate steps. Once proven, a new hypothesis §1 is added to your context for the rest of the proof.\n\nYou are not limited to basic equalities (§2). You can use §3 for any proposition, such as modular equivalences (§4), divisibility (§5), or predicates like §6.\n\n\n**Important:** In this game, the assignment syntax (§7) is disabled. You must state the assumption and provide the proof on the following line.\n\n**Using a proof block:**\nYou can state the assumption and provide the proof on the following lines. This sets your intermediate assumption as the current goal:\n§8\n§9":
