 "Now the other direction: if there exist integers §0 with §1, does that mean §2?\n\nYes — and to prove it, remember §3 from World 1: *every* integer is divisible by §4. So the \"common divisor\" half of the definition (§5 and §6) comes completely for free! All that's left is to hand back the Bézout identity you were already given.":
